-- Q5406: State and Local Government [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB 14 (as amended by GASB 61), a component unit is blended when its governing body is substantively the same as the primary government and it provides services exclusively to that government. The Building Authority meets both criteria. The Convention Bureau serves the public, so it is discretely presented.
Wrong (A): Discrete presentation for both ignores that the Building Authority''s board composition and exclusive service to the city require blending.
Wrong (B): Blending both ignores that the Convention Bureau serves the general public, not exclusively the city, disqualifying it from blended treatment.
Wrong (D): This reverses the correct treatment; the Building Authority qualifies for blending while the Convention Bureau does not.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 5406;

