-- Q5412: State and Local Government [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, paragraph 100, capital contributions from developers are reported separately after nonoperating revenues and expenses on the proprietary fund statement. They are not operating revenues because they do not arise from the fund''s principal ongoing operations.
Wrong (A): Capital contributions are nonrecurring and unrelated to ongoing service delivery; they do not qualify as operating revenue under GASB 34.
Wrong (C): Capital contributions flow through the operating statement (after nonoperating items), not directly to net position bypassing the statement.
Wrong (D): Contributed infrastructure is a capital asset addition, not a reduction to operating expenses.$EXPL$
