-- Q7648: Public Company Reporting [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 260-10-45-28, unvested RSUs are treated similarly to options under the treasury stock method. Assumed proceeds equal the average unrecognized compensation ($180,000). Shares repurchased = $180,000 / $60 = 3,000. Incremental shares = 12,000 - 3,000 = 9,000.
Wrong (A): 12,000 includes all RSUs without subtracting the 3,000 shares assumed repurchased from unrecognized compensation proceeds.
Wrong (C): 3,000 represents only the shares assumed repurchased, not the net incremental shares added to the denominator.
Wrong (D): 6,000 does not correspond to any valid step in the treasury stock method calculation for these RSUs.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7648;

-- Q7649: Public Company Reporting [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 260-10-45-40, when convertible securities are actually converted during the period, resulting shares are included in basic EPS from the conversion date (10,000 shares x 6/12 = 5,000 weighted shares). For diluted EPS, the if-converted method assumes conversion at the beginning of the period with interest saved added back net of tax.
Wrong (B): Including 10,000 shares for the full year overstates basic EPS; shares are weighted from the actual conversion date, not the beginning.
Wrong (C): Diluted EPS still requires the if-converted adjustment for the pre-conversion period even though actual conversion occurred.
Wrong (D): Basic EPS uses 10,000 shares weighted for 6 months (5,000), not 10,000 weighted for 6 months (which would be the same but the choice states it incorrectly as starting from the wrong share count).$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7649;

-- Q7651: Public Company Reporting [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 260-10-45-10, repurchased shares are removed from the weighted-average calculation from the repurchase date. Without repurchase: EPS = $750,000 / 250,000 = $3.00. With repurchase: weighted-average shares = 250,000 - (50,000 x 6/12) = 225,000, yielding $3.33.
Wrong (B): Treasury stock repurchases do not reduce the numerator (net income); they reduce the denominator (weighted-average shares), increasing EPS.
Wrong (C): Repurchased shares are removed from the weighted-average from the repurchase date, so the share count and EPS are affected.
Wrong (D): $3.75 incorrectly removes 50,000 shares for the full year (200,000 shares) rather than weighting from the July 1 repurchase date.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7651;
